('literature', 5, 'What is the concept of intertextuality theorized by Julia Kristeva?', 'The idea that every text is a fabric of references to other texts', ARRAY['The impossibility of original creation', 'The relationship between author and reader', 'Conscious plagiarism between writers'], 'en', true, 'Kristeva defined intertextuality in 1966 inspired by Bakhtin''s work.'),
('literature', 5, 'Who wrote If on a winter''s night a traveler?', 'Italo Calvino', ARRAY['Umberto Eco', 'Jorge Luis Borges', 'Jose Saramago'], 'en', true, 'Calvino published this metanovel in 1979, where the reader is the main character.'),
('literature', 5, 'What is the name of the experimental literary group founded by Raymond Queneau?', 'Oulipo', ARRAY['The Nouveau Roman', 'Tel Quel', 'The Grand Game'], 'en', true, 'Oulipo (Workshop of Potential Literature) was founded in 1960.'),
('literature', 5, 'Which British literary prize rewards the best novel in English?', 'The Booker Prize', ARRAY['The Pulitzer Prize', 'The National Book Award', 'The Prix Goncourt'], 'en', true, 'The Booker Prize has been awarded annually since 1969.'),
('literature', 5, 'What is Roland Barthes'' concept of the Death of the Author?', 'The idea that a text''s meaning does not depend on the author''s intention but on the reader', ARRAY['The end of literature as an art form', 'The symbolic suicide of the writer', 'The impossibility of writing after Auschwitz'], 'en', true, 'Barthes published The Death of the Author in 1967, a foundational essay in literary theory.'),
('literature', 5, 'Who received the first Prix Goncourt in 1903?', 'John-Antoine Nau', ARRAY['Marcel Proust', 'Emile Zola', 'Andre Gide'], 'en', true, 'John-Antoine Nau won the first Goncourt for Force ennemie.'),
('literature', 5, 'Who wrote The Man Without Qualities?', 'Robert Musil', ARRAY['Thomas Mann', 'Hermann Broch', 'Stefan Zweig'], 'en', true, 'Musil worked on this unfinished novel from 1930 until his death in 1942.'),
('literature', 5, 'What narrative technique did James Joyce use extensively in Ulysses?', 'Stream of consciousness', ARRAY['Classical interior monologue', 'Omniscient narration', 'Multiple points of view'], 'en', true, 'Joyce uses stream of consciousness to transcribe the flow of his characters'' thoughts.'),
('literature', 5, 'Who wrote Ficciones (Fictions)?', 'Jorge Luis Borges', ARRAY['Julio Cortazar', 'Gabriel Garcia Marquez', 'Ernesto Sabato'], 'en', true, 'Borges published this collection of short stories in 1944, blending philosophy and fantasy.'),
